# ---- Citable table: short-let planning permission by council (4 Nov 2026) ----
# Pulls together the planning position already on each council page (CX[...]['ctrl'], sourced there), one status + short summary per council.
# Status is set by hand below from each page's ctrl text; councils not listed get their nation's default line (same facts as the ENPL/WPL/NOCA text).
# Directory-only councils (PICK_EXCL) are left out. Also writes a CSV copy for journalists/researchers.
import csv as _csv,io as _io,html as _H0
PMGH='https://www.gov.uk/guidance/letting-out-a-self-catering-holiday-home-in-england-rules-and-regulations'
PMF='short-let-planning-permission-by-council.html';PMCSV='short-let-planning-permission-by-council.csv'
PMST={'in':('Permission needed (area rule in force)','p-in'),'pol':('Local planning policy in force','p-coming'),'prop':('Proposed or under review','p-proposed'),'case':('Case by case','p-announced')}
PMDEF={'England':('case','No short-let control area or Article 4 direction for holiday lets found. England has no short-let use class, so the council decides case by case whether letting a whole home is a material change of use.'),
 'Scotland':('case','No control area. You may still need planning permission if the planning authority considers the let a material change of use, so check before applying for a licence.'),
 'Wales':('case','No Article 4 direction or local short-let planning control found. Changes between C3 (main home), C5 (second home) and C6 (short-term let) are permitted development.')}
PM={
 'city-of-edinburgh':('in','The whole city has been a short-term let control area since 5 Sep 2022. Using a whole dwelling that isn\'t your main home as a short-term let very likely needs planning permission.'),
 'highland':('in','Badenoch &amp; Strathspey ward is a control area (since 4 Mar 2024). On 28 Sep 2026 the council agreed to send Scottish Ministers proposals for Inverness City and Highland Rural control areas (proposals only, not in force).'),
 'greater-london-all-boroughs':('in','Letting a whole home short term for more than 90 nights in a calendar year needs planning permission (Deregulation Act 2015, s44). <a href="london-90-night-counter.html">Count your nights</a>.'),
 'gwynedd':('in','Inside Eryri National Park, an Article 4 direction (in force since 1 Jun 2025) means changing a main home (C3) into a second home (C5) or short-term let (C6), or switching between C5 and C6, needs planning permission. Outside the park, Cyngor Gwynedd\'s own direction was quashed and is not in force.'),
 'conwy':('in','Inside Eryri National Park (part of Conwy), the park\'s Article 4 direction (since 1 Jun 2025) means changing a main home into a second home or short-term let needs planning permission. None found for the rest of Conwy.'),
 'blackpool':('pol','The council says most Airbnb-style holiday lets need planning permission: self-contained holiday flats and houses with no on-site management are a sui generis use. Outside the Town Centre, Resort Core and 6 Holiday Accommodation Areas, permission "generally will not be granted".'),
 'sefton':('pol','Short Term Holiday Lets SPD (adopted 5 Dec 2024): a home let whole to one family-sized group is unlikely to need permission, but letting rooms separately, adding bedrooms or larger groups is likely to. In Primarily Residential Areas a conversion is refused if 5% of properties within 100 m are already short lets, flats or HMOs.'),
 'oxford':('pol','Local Plan 2036 Policies V5 and H5: new short-stay accommodation only in set locations and with no loss of a home. A planning inspector upheld an enforcement notice against a Headington house run as a short-term let (11 Dec 2024).'),
 'cambridge':('pol','Local Plan 2018 Policy 3 allows changing housing to other uses only in exceptional circumstances; in Jan 2018 officers recommended enforcement notices against 13 flats used as short-term visitor accommodation. Draft Greater Cambridge Local Plan Policy J/VA would go further (not in force).'),
 'isles-of-scilly':('pol','Local Plan 2015-2030: converting a property for tourism must not lose homes available for permanent occupation unless there are wider public benefits (Policy WC5), and replacement dwellings, extensions or alterations must not include self-contained holiday letting accommodation unless already lawful (Policy LC8).'),
 'great-yarmouth':('pol','Local Plan Part 2 Policy L1 works the other way: in Holiday Accommodation Areas the council resists changing holiday accommodation to non-tourist uses. New holiday units usually carry holiday-only conditions.'),
 'teignbridge':('pol','Local Plan 2020-2040 (adopted 19 May 2026): new-build homes in Bishopsteignton, Dawlish, Shaldon, Stokeinteignhead and Teignmouth must be a primary residence, so not second homes or holiday lets (existing homes not affected). Inside Dartmoor National Park, new holiday lets get holiday-only conditions.'),
 'west-devon':('pol','Inside Dartmoor National Park, the park\'s Local Plan (Policy 5.5) only allows new short-stay holiday accommodation in villages, hamlets and countryside by converting suitable buildings, with holiday-only conditions. No holiday-let policy found outside the park.'),
 'derbyshire-dales':('pol','Inside the Peak District National Park, Policy DMR3 restricts new self-catering accommodation outside named settlements to holiday use. A draft primary residence clause on new housing is not adopted.'),
 'chichester':('pol','In West Wittering parish, Neighbourhood Plan Policy WW5 (made 28 Nov 2023) only supports new open-market homes limited to use as a principal residence. Elsewhere, decided case by case; no district-wide holiday-let policy found.'),
 'argyll-and-bute':('prop','Consultation (21 Sep to 15 Nov 2026) on a control area covering Mull and Iona; Coll and Tiree; Islay, Jura and Colonsay; and Oban, Lorn and the Inner Isles. Not in force.'),
 'fife':('prop','The council consulted on the principle of control areas (16 Jun to 8 Sep 2025); any designation needs Scottish Ministers\' approval. Reports that St Andrews and the East Neuk were chosen: '+U+'.'),
 'liverpool':('prop','Submission Draft Local Plan 2043 Policy TC7 would only support new short-term lets where fewer than 10% of properties within 100 m are HMOs and there is no over-concentration of short lets, with a management plan. Not examined or adopted.'),
 'rother':('prop','Proposed Submission Local Plan 2025-2042 (consultation 12 Oct to 24 Nov 2026): principal-residence-only for some new countryside homes, and proposals that lose homes to holiday accommodation not supported in Camber, Rye, Rye Foreign and Icklesham. Not in force.'),
 'city-of-york':('prop','The council says you may need planning permission and should get advice before taking bookings. Draft short-term holiday lets planning guidance (June 2026) still needs approval, so it is not in force.'),
 'brighton-and-hove':('prop','The council says you might need permission depending on how much the use changes. Zones where short lets are allowed or restricted are being looked at for City Plan 2041; nothing new applies yet.'),
 'bournemouth-christchurch-and-poole':('prop','A 2026 Full Council motion asks officers to investigate whether homes let for more than 90 nights a year are a material change of use and to gather evidence for a possible Article 4 direction. Nothing decided.'),
 'bristol':('prop','Draft Local Plan 2022-2040 Policy H2 would refuse the loss of an existing home, with narrow exceptions; adoption expected late 2026. Whether the main modifications change H2: '+U+'.'),
 'new-forest':('prop','The National Park Authority\'s draft Local Plan (Aug 2026) proposes a principal residence condition on all net new open-market homes in the Park. Not adopted; would not apply to existing homes.'),
 'manchester':('case','No control area or Article 4 direction for holiday lets. A 2024 council report says planning law does not currently require a change of use for a home to be used as a short-term let; the new Local Plan has no short-let policy.'),
 'lancaster':('case','No control area or Article 4 direction for holiday lets. Article 4 covers small HMOs in named Lancaster wards (since 10 Nov 2021) and minor works in conservation areas; whole-home short lets are decided case by case.'),
 'high-peak':('pol','Inside the Peak District National Park, Policy DMR3 restricts new self-catering accommodation outside named settlements to holiday use. Outside the park, no holiday-let Article 4; conservation-area Article 4s cover minor works only.'),
 'bath-and-north-east-somerset':('case','No control area or Article 4 direction for holiday lets. A 2018 council report said most short lets in Bath (3 or fewer rooms) stay in the C3 home use class; larger ones can be a material change of use.'),
 'west-lothian':('case','No control area, but every licence application must include planning permission or a certificate of lawfulness (or one confirming no material change of use).'),
 'inverclyde':('case','No control area. Check with planning before applying: where permission is needed and not obtained, the council can refuse the licence application within 14 days with no refund.'),
 'east-lothian':('case','No control area. If you apply for a licence without planning permission or a certificate you need, the council will refuse to consider the application.'),
}
_pmc=[c for c in d['councils'] if c['verified'] and _sl(c) not in PICK_EXCL and _sl(c) in CX]
assert all(k in {_sl(c) for c in _pmc} for k in PM),'PM slug not a listed council'
def _pmrow(c):
    s=_sl(c);st,tx=PM.get(s) or PMDEF[c['nation']];srcs=CX[s]['ctrl'][1] or {'England':[PMGH],'Scotland':[MG_CA],'Wales':['https://www.legislation.gov.uk/wsi/2022/994/article/2/made']}[c['nation']]
    return dict(slug=s,name=c['name'],nation=c['nation'],st=st,tx=tx,src=srcs[0])
PMR=sorted([_pmrow(c) for c in _pmc],key=lambda r:(r['nation'],r['name'].replace('City of ','')))
_pmn={k:sum(1 for r in PMR if r['st']==k) for k in PMST}
_pmsp=lambda k:f'<span class="pill {PMST[k][1]}">{PMST[k][0]}</span>'
def _pmtr(r):
    return f'<tr><td><a href="councils/{r["slug"]}.html">{e(r["name"])}</a></td><td>{r["nation"]}</td><td>{_pmsp(r["st"])}</td><td>{r["tx"]} <a href="{e(r["src"])}" rel="nofollow">Source</a></td></tr>'
_pmhd='<tr><th>Council</th><th>Nation</th><th>Status</th><th>What applies (summary)</th></tr>'
_pmorder={'in':0,'pol':1,'prop':2,'case':3}
_pmkey=sorted([r for r in PMR if r['slug'] in PM and r['st']!='case'],key=lambda r:(_pmorder[r['st']],r['nation'],r['name'].replace('City of ','')))
_pmtot=len(PMR)
PMQ=[('Do I need planning permission for a short-term let in the UK?','It depends on where the property is. In England there is no short-let use class, so your council decides case by case whether letting a whole home is a material change of use, and in Greater London letting a whole home for more than 90 nights a calendar year needs permission. In Scotland, a whole dwelling that is not your main home in a short-term let control area very likely needs permission. In Wales, moving between main home (C3), second home (C5) and short-term let (C6) is permitted development unless an Article 4 direction applies.'),
 ('Which UK councils have short-term let control areas?','Scotland has two control areas in force: the whole City of Edinburgh and the Badenoch and Strathspey ward of Highland (mygov.scot). Argyll and Bute is consulting on one, and Highland has sent proposals for Inverness City and Highland Rural control areas to Scottish Ministers; these are not in force.'),
 ('Where in Wales do you need planning permission to turn a home into a holiday let?','Inside Eryri (Snowdonia) National Park, an Article 4 direction in force since 1 June 2025 means changing a main home into a second home or short-term let needs planning permission. Cyngor Gwynedd\'s own direction for the rest of Gwynedd was quashed by the High Court. We found no other Welsh Article 4 direction on short lets among the councils we cover.'),
 ('Does Blackpool need planning permission for holiday lets?','Blackpool Council says most Airbnb-style holiday lets need planning permission, because self-contained holiday flats and houses with no on-site management are a sui generis use, and that outside the Town Centre, Resort Core and six Holiday Accommodation Areas permission generally will not be granted.'),
 ('Can I use or quote this table?','Yes. Please credit the UK Short-Let Rules Tracker and link to this page. Each row links to the official source and to the council page with the full wording. It is a summary of general information, not legal or planning advice, so always check with the council before relying on it.')]
_pmfaq='<div class="faq">'+''.join(f'<details><summary>{e(q)}</summary><p>{e(a)}</p></details>' for q,a in PMQ)+'</div>'
_pmfld='<script type="application/ld+json">'+json.dumps({'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'FAQPage','mainEntity':[{'@type':'Question','name':q,'acceptedAnswer':{'@type':'Answer','text':a}} for q,a in PMQ]}).replace('</','<\\/')+'</script>'
_pmld=json.dumps({'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Dataset','name':'Short-let planning permission by council (UK)','description':f'Planning position for short-term and holiday lets in {_pmtot} UK council areas: control areas, Article 4 directions, the London 90-night rule and local planning policies, each with an official source.','url':SITE+PMF,'dateModified':C,'creator':{'@type':'Organization','name':'The UK Short-Let Rules team','url':SITE},'spatialCoverage':'United Kingdom','isAccessibleForFree':True,'distribution':[{'@type':'DataDownload','encodingFormat':'text/csv','contentUrl':SITE+PMCSV}]}).replace('</','<\\/')
_bf=_io.StringIO();_w=_csv.writer(_bf)
_w.writerow(['council','nation','status','summary','council_page','official_source','checked'])
for r in PMR:_w.writerow([r['name'],r['nation'],PMST[r['st']][0],_H0.unescape(re.sub(r'<[^>]+>','',r['tx'])),SITE+'councils/'+r['slug'],r['src'],C])
open(PMCSV,'w',newline='').write(_bf.getvalue())
_pmt=f'Which councils need planning permission for short lets?'
_pmb=(ANSWER(_pmt,f'Only a few UK areas have a planning rule that covers short lets across the area: the City of Edinburgh and part of Highland (control areas), Greater London (over 90 nights a year) and, in Wales, Eryri National Park (Article 4 direction). Elsewhere your council decides case by case whether a let is a material change of use, and some councils have local policies. Of the {_pmtot} council areas below, {_pmn["in"]} have an area rule in force (in all or part), {_pmn["pol"]} have a local planning policy in force and {_pmn["prop"]} have a proposal or review under way.')
 +PICK('planning-table',aid='top-alerts',tag='div')
 +'<h2 id="specific-rules">Councils with a specific planning rule or proposal</h2><p>Each row summarises the planning section of the council page, with its official source. Statuses: '+' '.join(_pmsp(k) for k in ('in','pol','prop'))+'.</p>'
 +f'<div class="tw"><table class="stk pmt">{_pmhd}{"".join(_pmtr(r) for r in _pmkey)}</table></div>'
 +'<h2 id="national-rules">The national rules behind the table</h2><ul>'
 +f'<li><b>England:</b> no short-let use class (the C5 proposal is not law). <a href="{PMGH}" rel="nofollow">GOV.UK</a> says your local planning authority decides, based on how the property is used and its impact on neighbours. Greater London: more than 90 nights a calendar year needs permission (<a href="https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2015/20/section/44" rel="nofollow">Deregulation Act 2015, s44</a>). <a href="england-holiday-let-planning-permission.html">England planning guide</a>.</li>'
 +f'<li><b>Scotland:</b> councils can designate short-term let control areas. Inside one, a new short-term let very likely needs planning permission; outside, you may still need it if the let is a material change of use (<a href="{MG_CA}" rel="nofollow">mygov.scot</a>). <a href="scotland.html">Scotland rules</a>.</li>'
 +'<li><b>Wales:</b> use classes C3 (main home), C5 (second home) and C6 (short-term let) since Oct 2022; changes between them are permitted development unless an Article 4 direction applies (<a href="https://www.legislation.gov.uk/wsi/2022/994/article/2/made" rel="nofollow">WSI 2022/994</a>). <a href="wales.html">Wales rules</a>.</li>'
 +'<li><b>Northern Ireland:</b> no council pages yet. Belfast City Council is consulting (to 16 Nov 2026) on draft planning guidance for short-term lets; elsewhere, check with your council planning office. <a href="northern-ireland.html">Northern Ireland rules</a>.</li></ul>'
 +f'<h2 id="all-councils">All {_pmtot} council areas</h2><p>Every council area we cover, with its status. Open a council page for the full planning wording, key dates and a free alert when it changes.</p>'
 +COLLAPSE(f'Show all {_pmtot} council areas',f'<div class="tw"><table class="stk pmt">{_pmhd}{"".join(_pmtr(r) for r in PMR)}</table></div>',filt='Filter by council or nation')
 +f'<h2 id="cite">Use this table</h2><div class="box"><p>Journalists, agents and researchers are welcome to quote or link to this table. Please credit: <i>UK Short-Let Rules Tracker, "Short-let planning permission by council", {SITE}{PMF[:-5]}, checked {_fdate(C)}</i>.</p><p><a class="btn" href="{PMCSV}" download>Download the table (CSV)</a> <span class="small">Same rows as above, with the council page and official source for each.</span></p></div>'
 +'<h2 id="pm-faq">Common questions</h2>'+_pmfaq
 +'<p class="small">More: <a href="england-holiday-let-planning-permission.html">Holiday let planning permission in England</a> · <a href="london-90-night-counter.html">London 90-night counter</a> · <a href="england-short-term-let-rules-2027.html">England 2027 changes (C5, Article 4)</a> · <a href="buyer-due-diligence-checker.html">Buying a holiday let? Due-diligence checker</a> · <a href="councils.html">All councils</a> · <a href="changes.html">What changed</a>.</p>'
 +'<p class="small"><b>Not legal or planning advice.</b> Compiled by the UK Short-Let Rules team from each council page\'s official sources; summaries are shortened, so read the council page and ask the planning authority before acting. Items marked UNVERIFIED have not been confirmed against an official source.</p>'+FILTJS)
page(PMF,'Short-let planning permission by council (UK)',_pmb,desc='Which UK councils need planning permission for short lets? Control areas, Article 4 directions, London\'s 90 nights and local policies, with sources.',full_title='Short-let planning permission by council: UK table',head='<script type="application/ld+json">'+_pmld+'</script>'+_pmfld)
